    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0128" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.01/10–3148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tittmann</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"> niact   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-10-31T12:00:00-05:00">October 31,
                            1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>634. Department’s 411, October 30, 9 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d88-f1"/> Unless
                    instructed to contrary, I propose to establish contact with new Chief of
                    Government and Minister of Foreign Affairs within next 48 hours, basing my
                    actions on Bogotá Resolution. If asked whether such contact constitutes
                    recognition, I propose to quote paragraphs one and three of Bogotá Resolution
                    No. 35 without comment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tittmann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d88-f1" n="1" xml:id="d88-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; Acting Secretary Lovett indicated that the Department’s policy would
                    be to act in conformity with Bogotá Resolution 35 on continuity of diplomatic
                    relations (823.01/10–3048).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
